---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LeadForm from '../components/LeadForm.astro';
const title = "About Us | Star Martial Arts, Gainesville, FL";
const description = "Family-focused martial arts in Gainesville since 2006. Meet our team and learn the values behind every class at Star Martial Arts.";
const schema = [];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} image="/images/hero.webp" schema={schema} pageClass="pg-about">
<section class="ah"><div class="w kh"><div class="rv"><p class="bc"><a href="/">Home</a> / About Us</p><p class="lab eb">About Star Martial Arts</p><h1 class="d" style="font-size:clamp(48px,7vw,92px);margin:16px 0 20px">Making champions in life, since 2006.</h1><p class="lead" style="font-size:19px;max-width:560px">Star Martial Arts is a family-focused martial arts community in Gainesville, Florida, built on one idea: martial arts is a vehicle for developing strong leaders, healthy bodies, and champions in life.</p><div class="btns" style="margin-top:28px"><button class="btn p" data-gs>Get Started</button><a class="btn ow" href="#ab-values">Our Core Values</a></div></div>
<div class="im rv has-bgi"><img class="bgi" src="/images/hero.webp" alt="Star Martial Arts students and instructors gathered together on the mat" width="1600" height="1067" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" style="object-position:center 35%"></div></div></section>

<section class="sec"><div class="w"><p class="lab eb rv">Our story · Founded in 2006, growing into the future</p><h2 class="hdg rv" style="margin:14px 0 36px;max-width:16ch">Rooted in Gainesville. Built for the next generation.</h2>
<div class="sy"><div class="ps rv"><div class="im has-bgi" style="height:auto;aspect-ratio:1/1;width:100%;"><img class="bgi" src="/images/ed.webp" alt="Ed Gnad, founder of Star Martial Arts" width="770" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="object-position:center 20%"></div><div class="im has-bgi" style="height:auto;aspect-ratio:1/1;width:100%;"><img class="bgi" src="/images/jb.webp" alt="Justin Scoby, owner and operator" width="538" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="object-position:center 15%"></div></div>
<div class="rv"><p class="t">Star Martial Arts was founded in Gainesville, Florida, in 2006 by <b>Ed Gnad</b>.</p>
<p class="t">Ed’s own journey began in elementary school, when he was bullied and started martial arts at age seven to find his footing. He started training in Hawaii, and as his military family moved around the country, his training never stopped. He grew into a highly ranked competitor, earning a bronze medal at the world championships.</p>
<p class="t">In 2006, Mr. Gnad branched out on his own and opened Star Martial Arts. The goal of the school was simple: help kids find their confidence and learn real skills, so they could stand up for themselves, help others, and become bully proof.</p>
<p class="t">From the beginning, our mission has centered around using martial arts to develop strong leaders, healthy bodies, and champions in life.</p>
<p class="t">While martial arts is at the foundation of our organization, we’ve grown into something much larger than traditional martial arts classes. Our After School and Summer Camp programs have become major parts of how we serve Gainesville families, giving children opportunities to develop friendships, confidence, discipline, and valuable life skills.</p>
<p class="t">I joined the Star Martial Arts team in 2017 and purchased the organization at the end of 2025. I didn’t enter the business as an outside investor. I spent years working within the organization, learning its culture, working with students and families, and understanding what makes StarMA special.</p>
<p class="t">Today, we’re continuing to build on that foundation while modernizing and expanding the organization. An important milestone is the opening of our second location in North Gainesville in 2026, which lets us serve more families while maintaining the same core curriculum, culture, and standards.</p>
<p class="t">Our philosophy remains centered around the belief that martial arts can positively influence who a person becomes, not just what they can accomplish physically.</p>
<p style="font-weight:600;margin-top:8px">Justin Scoby, Current Owner</p></div></div>
<div class="pl g4" style="margin-top:44px"><div class="pi rv"><h3>2006</h3><p>Star Martial Arts is founded in Gainesville by Ed Gnad.</p></div><div class="pi rv"><h3>2017</h3><p>Justin Scoby joins the Star Martial Arts team.</p></div><div class="pi rv"><h3>End of 2025</h3><p>Justin Scoby becomes the owner of Star Martial Arts.</p></div><div class="pi rv"><h3>2026</h3><p>Our second location opens in North Gainesville.</p></div></div>
</div></section>

<section class="sec dk"><div class="w" style="max-width:860px"><p class="lab eb rv">Our mission</p><h2 class="hdg rv" style="margin:14px 0 24px">Strong leaders. Healthy bodies. Champions in life.</h2>
<div class="ms rv"><p>At Star Martial Arts, our mission is to use martial arts as a vehicle to develop strong leaders, healthy bodies, and champions in life.</p><p>Through discipline, accountability, and consistent growth, we teach our students that confidence is earned, pressure creates strength, and true success comes from doing the small things right every day.</p><p>By holding high standards in professionalism, communication, and personal responsibility, we prepare our students not just for success in martial arts, but for success in life.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="sec df" id="ab-values"><div class="w"><p class="lab eb rv">Our core values</p><h2 class="hdg rv" style="margin:14px 0 14px">Eight values. One standard.</h2><p class="sub rv">These guide how we teach, how we show up, and what we expect of ourselves. Our standards are high, and our support is higher.</p><div class="pl g4" style="margin-top:32px"><div class="pi rv"><p class="lab" style="color:var(--r);margin-bottom:6px">01</p><h3>Earned Confidence</h3><p>Nothing given. Everything earned.</p></div><div class="pi rv"><p class="lab" style="color:var(--r);margin-bottom:6px">02</p><h3>Early is on Time</h3><p>Preparation is one of the ways we show respect. We believe in being ready before we’re needed, honoring our commitments, and setting an example of reliability for the students and families who count on us.</p></div><div class="pi rv"><p class="lab" style="color:var(--r);margin-bottom:6px">03</p><h3>Pressure Makes Diamonds</h3><p>Handle the pressure, live a better life.</p></div><div class="pi rv"><p class="lab" style="color:var(--r);margin-bottom:6px">04</p><h3>Dress to Impress</h3><p>We take pride in how we represent ourselves and our team. A clean uniform, professional appearance, and attention to detail reflect the care and respect we bring to everything we do.</p></div><div class="pi rv"><p class="lab" style="color:var(--r);margin-bottom:6px">05</p><h3>Communication is Critical</h3><p>You change the way you communicate, you change your life.</p></div><div class="pi rv"><p class="lab" style="color:var(--r);margin-bottom:6px">06</p><h3>1% Growth</h3><p>Find the 1% every class, every day.</p></div><div class="pi rv"><p class="lab" style="color:var(--r);margin-bottom:6px">07</p><h3>Quality over Quantity</h3><p>Details make or break progress.</p></div><div class="pi rv"><p class="lab" style="color:var(--r);margin-bottom:6px">08</p><h3>Professionalism Comes First</h3><p>We take accountability. We take care of our members.</p></div></div></div></section>

<section class="sec"><div class="w"><p class="lab eb rv">Our culture</p><h2 class="hdg rv" style="margin:14px 0 32px">A place where everyone belongs</h2><div class="pl g4">
<div class="pi rv"><h3>We Over Me</h3><p>Students learn to lift each other up. Teamwork, kindness, and effort are what we celebrate.</p></div>
<div class="pi rv"><h3>Members First</h3><p>We take accountability and take care of our members. Every decision starts with what is best for students and families.</p></div>
<div class="pi rv"><h3>Active Supervision</h3><p>Our team stays engaged and aware. Never just stand there.</p></div>
<div class="pi rv"><h3>Families Grow Together</h3><p>Our life skills program brings families and students together, so parents stay part of their child’s progress.</p></div></div></div></section>

<section class="sec dk"><div class="w kb"><div class="rv"><p class="lab eb">Student development</p><h2 class="hdg" style="margin:14px 0 16px">Committed to the whole student</h2><p style="font-size:18px;color:#E4E4E4">We care about who students become, not just the belt around their waist.</p><ul><li>Martial arts that builds real skill, with every belt earned</li><li>Life skills taught on purpose, through Mat Chats and daily practice</li><li>Families included in the conversation</li><li>Progress celebrated in class, at school, and at home</li></ul><p style="margin-top:22px"><a href="/after-school-program/" style="font-weight:600;color:#fff">Read Matthias’s story →</a></p></div>
<div class="im rv has-bgi"><img class="bgi" src="/images/g3.webp" alt="An instructor talking with a circle of seated students" width="700" height="467" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div></section>

<section class="sec"><div class="w"><p class="lab eb rv">Our team</p><h2 class="hdg rv" style="margin:14px 0 14px">The people who make StarMA possible</h2><p class="sub rv" style="margin-bottom:32px">Get to know the people who will be working with your child.</p>
<article class="tm rv" style="grid-template-columns:280px 1fr"><div class="im has-bgi" style="height:auto;aspect-ratio:3/4;width:100%;"><img class="bgi" src="/images/jk.webp" alt="Justin Scoby performing a high kick" width="640" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="object-position:center 30%"></div><div><h3 class="d">Justin Scoby</h3><p class="rl">Owner / Operator</p><p>Justin joined StarMA in 2017 and became the owner at the end of 2025. He brings a blend of technical expertise, competitive experience, and genuine heart to every class he teaches. A proud University of Florida graduate with a B.A. in Business Administration and a specialization in Sports Management, his academic and martial arts journey reflects a lifelong commitment to growth, for himself and for his students. His mission: help every student walk out of class stronger, more confident, and proud of what they’ve accomplished.</p><div class="chips"><span>3rd Degree Black Belt, Taekwondo</span><span>1st Degree Black Belt, Kickboxing</span><span>US Open Sparring Champion</span><span>Inaugural Hyper Black Belt</span></div></div></article>
<div class="tg"><article class="tm rv"><div class="im has-bgi" style="height:auto;aspect-ratio:3/4;width:100%;"><img class="bgi" src="/images/sg.webp" alt="Sage Bachus, Lead Instructor" width="600" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="object-position:center 25%"></div><div><h3 class="d">Sage Bachus</h3><p class="rl">Lead Instructor, West Gainesville</p><p>Sage has trained in taekwondo for 13 years and holds a 4th degree black belt. His martial arts journey began in Colorado, and after his family moved to Gainesville, he found a home at Star Martial Arts. He is one of two members of the inaugural class of Hyper Black Belts, earning his 1st degree black belt in kickboxing. Sage graduated from the University of Florida in 2025 with a bachelor’s degree in engineering. He is a committed member of our team, excited to work with the next generation of leaders and inspire students to take charge and lead their generation.</p><div class="chips"><span>4th Degree Black Belt</span><span>1st Degree Black Belt, Kickboxing</span><span>Inaugural Hyper Black Belt</span></div></div></article>
<article class="tm rv"><div class="im has-bgi" style="height:auto;aspect-ratio:3/4;width:100%;"><img class="bgi" src="/images/cg.webp" alt="Cristian Gomez, Lead Instructor, North Gainesville" width="600" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="object-position:center 25%"></div><div><h3 class="d">Cristian Gomez</h3><p class="rl">Lead Instructor, North Gainesville</p><p>Cristian’s StarMA story began as a student. He joined our kickboxing program at age 16, and his positivity and smile brightened every class he was in. Once we saw his potential, he joined our instructor team and has steadily worked his way up through the ranks to Lead Instructor at our North Gainesville location.</p><p>An accomplished competitor, Cristian’s boxing background makes him the expert in our striking program. Because he grew up in our program, he understands what it feels like to be a new student, and he brings that perspective, along with the same positive energy, to every class he teaches.</p><div class="chips"><span>2nd Degree Black Belt</span></div></div></article></div>
</div></section>

<section class="sec df"><div class="w"><p class="lab eb rv">Two Gainesville locations</p><h2 class="hdg rv" style="margin:14px 0 28px">Come see us</h2><div class="lc2">
<div class="pi rv"><h3>West Gainesville</h3><p>500 NW 60th St, Suite A<br>Gainesville, FL 32607<br><a href="tel:3525051499">352-505-1499</a><br><a href="mailto:westgv@mystarma.com">westgv@mystarma.com</a></p></div>
<div class="pi rv"><h3>North Gainesville</h3><p>5000 NW 34th Blvd, Suite 5<br>Gainesville, FL 32605<br><a href="tel:3526726356">352-672-6356</a><br><a href="mailto:northgv@mystarma.com">northgv@mystarma.com</a></p></div></div></div></section>

<LeadForm page="about" />
<section class="sec fin"><div class="w rv"><h2>Come see what we’re about</h2><p>Every child deserves a chance, a place to belong, and someone who believes in them.</p><div class="btns"><button class="btn p" data-gs>Get Started</button><a class="btn ow" href="/after-school-program/">After School</a><a class="btn ow" href="/summer-camp/">Summer Camp</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
